xorxes: I'd go with "sraji".

*sraji*
*x1 is vertical/upright/erect/plumb/oriented straight up and down in 
reference frame/gravity x2.*

What are the various things that work as a "reference frame"?

xorxes: I wouldn't restrict it to lines. A line can be perpendicular to a 
plane, and also it should be usable with general objects.

If you think sraji works, 
then I suggest that it could be used for general objects, 
and a different word could be used for lines and planes.
The relationship of two lines or planes forming 
four equal angles seems unique.

xorxes: For your full description I think it's more clear to use three 
separate predicates.

I formed a similar thought.

